<article class="env-definition" id="0DNW">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DNW">Definition <span data-tag="0DNW">106.8.1</span>.</a> A morphism $f : \mathcal{X} \to \mathcal{Y}$ of algebraic stacks is said to be <em>formally smooth</em> if it is formally smooth on objects as a $1$-morphism in categories fibred in groupoids as explained in Criteria for Representability, Section <a href="/tag/06CZ" data-tag="06CZ">97.6</a>. </p>
